From 77f402386fdb50bef1b3527ecfa177799efd8bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:02:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(app): recognise pockets and slots and turn them into
 operations

A new app module, recognize, reads a model's planar-face topology for
flat floors whose outer ring has walls rising into them on opposite
sides: closed pockets, open pockets, and straight slots with open,
round or square ends. Each answer carries the floor's ring, floor and
top Z, depth, area, tightest inside corner, open spans, island count
and, for a slot, its centreline ends, width and length. Degenerate
facets never weld; a missing or empty model is refused by name.

recognize::operation_for maps one onto CreateOperation's inputs: a 2D
Pocket on a pick of the floor face (depths relative to the selection,
so they follow a moved part), or a Slot along the centreline for a slot
with no square closed end. The MCP tool detect_pockets lists them and,
with create, adds the operation as one undo step.

The GUI entry point is #511. Recognised slots inherit #510 (every
typed Slot riding its cap is convicted of a gouge today).

Fixes #35

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
